attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 10, `hypA` to `ascB`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 4% of calls {S1}. The model names 7 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 6, `hycF`, 7% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at column 11**, `ascF`, carried by 89% {S2.c11}. Then the long spine, columns 12 to 61, `ascG` to `glaH`, [[formate hydrogenlyase]] at columns 1 to 9 and [[sorbitol glucitol transporter]] at columns 21 to 24 {S3, Q}. The last stretch, columns 62 to 79, is the most plastic of the window, in a region of plasticity in 31 to 51% of calls {S4, P}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 78%, and hesitates less there, 0.16 against 1.23 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 62, is a fork column, at 2.73 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on variable columns.** Columns 68 to 79, `recN` to `dgcN`, are carried by 19 to 57% of chromosomes, all persistent {S4.c68-79}. The last column is `dgcN`, in 19% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.41 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 2.29 against 0.18 bits, and names fewer genes, 53% against 96% {C}.

